{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>Because you did not serve HaShem your Elohim with joy.</b> Scripture holds them to account for serving the Master, may He be exalted, when the service was not done with joy — for a person is obligated for joy when engaged in commandments, and joy in the performance of a commandment is itself a commandment in its own right. Aside from the reward one receives for the commandment, one receives reward for the joy; therefore He punishes here the one who performs the service of a commandment when he did not do it with joy. Therefore a person must perform the commandments with joy and wholehearted intention. Thus they said in the Midrash of Ruth: if Reuben had known that the Holy One, blessed be He, records concerning him (Genesis 37:21) ״וישמע ראובן ויצלהו מידם״, he would have carried him on his shoulders to his father; and if Aaron had known that the Holy One, blessed be He, records concerning him (Exodus 4:14) ״וראך ושמח בלבו״, he would have gone out to meet him with timbrels and dances; and if Boaz had known that the Holy One, blessed be He, records concerning him (Ruth 2:14) ״ותאכל ותשבע ותותר״, he would have fed her fatted calves."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:51:42.369115379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}